From 8b44457f724facec4706a15849c648d224f72264 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Janota <Roman.Janota@cesnet.cz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 17:40:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sn UPDATE asynchronous on-change resync

A resync and the sync-on-start update were sent synchronously from the
caller's thread. A caller that is also the only reader of the pipe
blocks on a push-update larger than the pipe, and a caller serving
operational data waits for its own providers until they time out.

Every on-change subscription now has a sync worker. A resync only
requests a round and returns at once, it never waits for a round in
progress. A round holds the dampening lock across getting the data, so
every change committed after the snapshot is sent after it, and drops
a dampened change still pending, which the update supersedes and whose
patch ID is being reset. The sync-on-start update is requested once the
SR subscriptions exist, so no change in between is lost.

A failure to get the data is now only logged, not returned.

Upstream: https://github.com/sysrepo/sysrepo/commit/efec7ad136467b1bf1af57a48dbc24db6bea39d9
Signed-off-by: Mattias Walström <lazzer@gmail.com>
